{
  "summary": "This experiment tested ViT-L (imagenet_vit_l) as the image encoder in the multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool, weighted-fusion configuration, providing a clean single-variable comparison against the ResNet50 variant (llm_summary_008, acc ~0.678, F1 ~0.646). Validation accuracy improved to ~0.706 (F1: ~0.667), a gain of ~0.028 over ResNet50 and ~0.056 over the RNA-only scvi_n200 baseline (llm_summary_005, acc ~0.650), indicating in this controlled comparison that the stronger pretrained image encoder does unlock additional complementary signal beyond what ResNet50 contributed. It remains uncertain whether the observed gain reflects a fundamental ceiling on image information or is partly attributable to ViT-L's greater model capacity and pretraining scale, and whether alternative fusion mechanisms, different weighting schemes, or further encoder refinements could yield additional improvements on top of this new best configuration."
}

